/-!
# Three good exact colourings of `[1, 328]` (generated by `scripts/make_colourings.py`)

Point `x` gets the base-8 digit `x - 1` of the constant (`digitCol`). With `p = 109`, a point
`X ≢ 1 (mod 109)` has colour `0`, `1` or `2` according to the cubic residue class of `X - 1`
(`(X - 1)^36 mod 109` is `1`, `45` or `63`); the points `1, 110, 219, 328` have the colours
`0, 3, 3, 0` (`r = 4`), `3, 4, 3, 4` (`r = 5`) and `3, 4, 5, 3` (`r = 6`). The colour classes have
110, 108, 108, 2 points (`r = 4`);
108, 108, 108, 2, 2 points (`r = 5`);
108, 108, 108, 2, 1, 1 points (`r = 6`).

Point 1 first:

* `r = 4`:
  `0002022201212221001021102120221100011101201010012112220022211210010102101110001122`
  `0212011201001222121022202003002022201212221001021102120221100011101201010012112220`
  `0222112100101021011100011220212011201001222121022202003002022201212221001021102120`
  `2211000111012010100121122200222112100101021011100011220212011201001222121022202000`
* `r = 5`:
  `3002022201212221001021102120221100011101201010012112220022211210010102101110001122`
  `0212011201001222121022202004002022201212221001021102120221100011101201010012112220`
  `0222112100101021011100011220212011201001222121022202003002022201212221001021102120`
  `2211000111012010100121122200222112100101021011100011220212011201001222121022202004`
* `r = 6`:
  `3002022201212221001021102120221100011101201010012112220022211210010102101110001122`
  `0212011201001222121022202004002022201212221001021102120221100011101201010012112220`
